        "original_id": "eafd5ab9-7448-5038-9c67-24b757411107",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Awki, Jacabamba, Andes, South America\n- Topics: Mountain ranges, glaciers, climatic regimes\n\nFacts:\n- Awki lies southeast of Jacabamba.\n- The Andes, also called the Andean Mountains or Spanish \"Cordillera de los Andes,\" are the longest continental mountain range in the world.\n- The Andes extend north to south through Venezuela, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Bolivia, Argentina, and Chile.\n- Glaciers in South America develop exclusively on the Andes.\n- Glaciers in South America are subject to the Andes climatic regimes of the Tropical Andes, Dry Andes, and Wet Andes.",
